From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Strix Halo Packaging <packaging@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Backport: MiniMax-M3 video processor compatibility for Transformers 5.18

Upstream: vllm-project/vllm#59613, "[Bugfix] Fix minimax-m3 multimodal
processor compatability with Transformers v5.18", merge commit
b558f160a2c0abcb5902acc3c91a14c38a4af173 (main, 2026-10-02). v0.31.0 carries
the same one-line change on its release branch.

Transformers 5.18 no longer passes do_convert_rgb to
BaseVideoProcessor._preprocess, so the required positional parameter in
MiniMaxM3VLVideoProcessor._preprocess raises TypeError on the first video.
The parameter was unused; older Transformers still pass it and it now lands
in **kwargs.

Carried: the whole commit (vllm/transformers_utils/processors/minimax_m3.py),
unchanged.

Drop at the first packaged vLLM release whose
MiniMaxM3VLVideoProcessor._preprocess has no do_convert_rgb parameter.

---
diff --git a/vllm/transformers_utils/processors/minimax_m3.py b/vllm/transformers_utils/processors/minimax_m3.py
index 60fa7ed..b758c11 100644
--- a/vllm/transformers_utils/processors/minimax_m3.py
+++ b/vllm/transformers_utils/processors/minimax_m3.py
@@ -375,7 +375,6 @@ class MiniMaxM3VLVideoProcessor(BaseVideoProcessor):
     def _preprocess(
         self,
         videos: list[torch.Tensor],
-        do_convert_rgb: bool,
         do_resize: bool,
         size: SizeDict,
         resample: "PILImageResampling | InterpolationMode | int | None",
